{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>So you shall purge the blood of the innocent from Israel.</b> The punishment [required to expiate] the blood of the innocent, as it says: וְלָאָרֶץ לֹא יְכֻפַּר לַדָּם אֲשֶׁר שֻׁפַּךְ בָּהּ כִּי אִם בְּדַם שֹׁפְכוֹ (Numbers 35:33)." "<b>And it shall be well with you.</b> So that the murderer does not go on to kill others, and וְהַנִּשְׁאָרִים יִשְׁמְעוּ וְיִירָאוּ (Deuteronomy 19:20)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The lemma phrase עֹנֶשׁ דַּם הַנָּקִי is read as 'the punishment for the blood of the innocent,' i.e., the punishment that the shed blood demands; the word עֹנֶשׁ could also be rendered more narrowly as 'penalty.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:21:49.323532374Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}